\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Group-relative baseline and advantage}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{grpo}
\tag{credit-assignment}

\p{Let #{r_i=R_V(x,y^{(i)})} be the rewards in a rollout group. Define the
group mean and stabilized standard deviation by}

##{
  \bar r=\frac1g\sum_{i=1}^g r_i,
  \qquad
  s_\varepsilon=
  \sqrt{\frac1g\sum_{i=1}^g(r_i-\bar r)^2+\varepsilon},
  \qquad \varepsilon>0.
}

\p{The \strong{group-relative advantage} of response #{i} is}

##{
  \widehat A_i=\frac{r_i-\bar r}{s_\varepsilon}.
}

\p{Section 4.1.2 of \citef{shao2024deepseekmath} normalizes group credit by
the reported group standard deviation. Adding #{\varepsilon} is an FTIP
stabilization convention, not a formula attributed to that source.
Implementations also differ on zero-variance groups and token weighting.}
